From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mcla-x86 SDK patch layer
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0810: resolve_elide: at a draw resolution scale above 1, no scaled-buffer store for dual-written resolves nothing reads back; copy_byte_census (Direct3D 12; native stream, zero-copy P1 + P3)

Source: Ours, written for this SDK (native stream; design note scratch/zerocopy/DESIGN.md, test plan scratch/zerocopy/TESTPLAN.md).
  Written without a build or a run: checked with clang++ 20.1.8 -fsyntax-only (the SDK's Release flags, from impl-Release.ninja) of
  the 4 changed or new translation units (d3d12/resolve_elide.cpp with resolve_defer.cpp's flags, d3d12/texture_cache.cpp,
  d3d12/render_target_cache.cpp, command_processor.cpp) and of 2 more that include the changed headers; 0 errors, no new warning.
  No shader, no DXBC. Applies after 0780 (and after 0760, whose dual write at scale it builds on).
Licence: GPL-3 (owner's own work, part of mcla-x86); the patched files are ReXGlue SDK code (BSD-3-Clause)
Purpose: At draw scale 2 (profile 2000p) a dual-written resolve (0760 scaled_copy_levers 1) writes its bytes twice: into the
  texture that samples them and into the scaled resolve buffer. The buffer is invisible to the guest CPU; its only readers are the
  loads of scaled_resolve textures (LoadTextureDataFromResidentMemoryImpl), the 1x copy of resolve_unscaled_copy_rules and the
  copy to the guest memory of readback_resolve_rules (both chosen by the resolve's rules, right after it), and
  resolve_dual_write_verify. The buffer copy is dead unless a load over the range comes before a later resolve writes those
  bytes again.
  New cvars (Direct3D 12, hot reload, all default to today's behaviour):
    resolve_elide (int 0..3, default 0): 1 learn (every store made; every scaled load is checked against records of the
      dual-written stores not yet overwritten whole; destinations read are logged in the rule grammar, with what 2 would have
      done: would-miss), 2 elide (the store of a dual-written resolve goes to a null view once resolve_elide_after of its
      resolves went by unread, unless an unscaled-copy / readback / keep rule matches, the texture was written in part and is
      outdated, or resolve_dual_write_verify is on; a load over an elided store is one wrong texture, logged as an ERROR
      `[resolve-elide] MISS`, and its destination is stored from then on), 3 elide + poison (each elided range filled with
      resolve_elide_poison_value by ClearUnorderedAccessViewUint).
    resolve_elide_min_kb (int, default 16384): 2 / 3 elide only stores at least this big (at 2000p the five full-screen
      resolves, which are 69 % of the dual-written class; 0 = every size); 1 reports every size,
    resolve_elide_after (int, default 60), resolve_elide_poison_value (uint, 0xFFFF00FF),
    resolve_elide_keep_rules (string, the grammar of readback_resolve_rules; defined in command_processor.cpp),
    copy_byte_census (bool, default false): `[copy-bytes] ...` every 10 s, host bytes a frame by class (resolve read / store /
      store elided / dual-written texture, texture load read / write; transfers and clears with 0811).
  Log: `[resolve-elide] <mode> over N frames ...` every 10 s while active, `[resolve-elide] read: addr=...,len=...,pitch=...,
  height=...,fmt=...,src=... - by the load of ...` once per destination, `[resolve-elide] at exit: ... as keep rules: ...` and
  up to 64 `[resolve-elide] at exit: addr=...: N stores (X a frame ...) of M MB each, ...` lines (the inventory of the
  dual-written resolves of the run, largest first).
  A record is retired when a later resolve with the same destination base, pitch and bytes a texel writes an area that
  contains it (the scaled tiled address is a one-to-one function of the texel and those three).
  New file src/graphics/d3d12/resolve_elide.cpp (listed in src/graphics/CMakeLists.txt) and include/rex/graphics/d3d12/
  copy_census.h; CommandProcessor::MatchResolveScaledBytesReader (no logging, own rule caches). No change to
  d3d12/command_processor.cpp.
Bucket: REDO

0810-resolve-elide-scaled-store.patch (mcla-x86 native stream, zero-copy P1).

